From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 08:55:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 163/167] hjviewer: the relogin notice says the key stays on
 its device
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

"로그인이 풀렸습니다" told the user that a device restored from a backup
does not get the security key. On an iPhone the key is a ThisDeviceOnly
Keychain item: an encrypted backup carries it, and a restore to the same
iPhone brings it back; only a backup restored to another device brings the
token without the key, the case drop_login sees (Android keeps the app's
files out of backups and transfers, Windows keeps the key out of the
roaming profile). The notice now says what the privacy statement says:
the security key stays on the device where the user logged in and does not
move to another device, even through a backup or restore. The comments in
the account code that read "a restored iPhone" now say a backup restored
to another device, and a test pins the two texts.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
